<urn:atm:triage:finding/RRG-TRUST-KEY-LOOPBACK-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RRG-TRUST-KEY-LOOPBACK-001" ;
  triage:title "self-send to <agent>@<team>.localhost dials loopback:43101 but the mTLS client config is selected by bare trust hostname, so a trust entry named localhost pinned to another daemon on 43102 shadows the local daemon and the send fails with an mTLS pin mismatch" ;
  triage:description "Reported by skillrx@hermes on rand-m5 at ~20:55Z on 2026-09-03 and independently by loki: atm send skillrx@hermes.localhost exits 3 RemoteDeliveryUnconfirmed with an mTLS pin mismatch. Sanitized facts: the local daemon on 43101 presents certificate fingerprint prefix BFCA while the enabled trust entry named localhost is pinned to fingerprint prefix 4E7B with https_port 43102 (an ssh tunnel to the Colima VM daemon); the send dialed localhost:43101 and verified against the 43102 pin. quality-mgr verdict 01M1MHGXV9KT656R81YSPZE8PK: product defect, Blocking for the readiness gate because it breaks the documented localhost smoke stage (the rand-m5 site/reports smoke rows for localhost and local-ip stages at 20260831T2032Z and 20260831T2035Z already FAILED for the same reason). Root cause: routing keys the self-send by address (is_legacy_direct_host short-circuits localhost to the loopback port without consulting peers) while trust keys by bare HostName (client_config_for matches candidate.authority == peer), so two different daemons that share the hostname literal localhost cannot be distinguished and a foreign entry silently shadows the local self-send route. Note that the trust entry itself is a harness isolation violation on rand-m5 (Colima peers must never be named localhost; being removed) and is the primary classification; this record is the secondary product record and stands on its own. Required fix shape per quality-mgr: key trust lookups the same way routing does (host plus https_port, or the resolved dial address), so an entry pinned for 43102 can never be consulted for a 43101 dial; as defense in depth, warn (not hard-reject, to avoid a startup regression on hosts that still carry such an entry) when an enabled trust entry declares a loopback literal host that collides with the local daemon's own self-send address. Closure bar: a regression test that seeds a trust entry named localhost on a non-local port with a foreign fingerprint and proves a localhost self-send still verifies against the local daemon; a test for the warning; no change to the frozen legacy synchronous daemon; the readiness localhost smoke stage passing on rand-m5 after the entry is removed and again with a deliberately colliding entry present. QA-4c update 2026-09-04T03:35Z (quality-mgr, code-only verdict, no host access): the code and regression-test halves of the closure bar are already satisfied on this branch as of commit 462370d3b (ancestor of 758d484b9, landed before this finding was even triaged): crates/peer-tls/src/lib.rs:270 client_config_for now matches candidate.authority == peer AND candidate.https_port == port against the actually-dialed TCP port; test rrg_trust_key_loopback_001_client_config_requires_exact_authority_port (lib.rs:767) seeds a foreign pin at localhost:43102 and a real pin at rand-m5.local:43101, proves a 43101 dial against the foreign-pinned localhost authority is rejected and a 43102 dial still succeeds; loopback_port_collisions (lib.rs:71-90) implements the warn-not-reject defense-in-depth, wired at adapter construction and covered by test loopback_port_collisions_returns_only_enabled_local_matches (lib.rs:603). Do not re-dispatch a code fix for this finding. What remains, and is the sole reason this record stays open: the record's own live-evidence bar (readiness localhost smoke stage passing on rand-m5 with the offending entry removed, and again with a deliberately colliding entry present) has not been run -- per standing project direction the rand-m5 host daemon stays at 1.4.10 for now, so this live proof is held pending that decision, not pending further code." ;
  triage:phaseId "readiness-1.4" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "peer-trust" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
